# The frontend's production image builds from the repo root, because the gcsim pin it needs
# lives in `docs/`. Everything here is what that context must not carry.
#
# **`frontend/.dockerignore` no longer applies.** A `.dockerignore` is resolved against the
# build *context*, so widening the context to the repo root retired that file silently — its
# `.env` exclusions included. Everything it held is repeated below — **prefixed `**/`**,
# because a `.dockerignore` pattern is matched against the whole relative path and is *not*
# implicitly recursive the way a `.gitignore` is. A bare `.env` would have excluded only the
# one at the context root and let `frontend/.env` through, which is precisely the file the old
# ignore was carrying.

# Version control and CI
.git
.gitignore
.github

# Secrets. `/home/ubuntu/mistilteinn/.env` holds POSTGRES_PASSWORD and DATABASE_URL, and it
# reached the Docker daemon the moment the context widened. Nothing COPYs it, so this was not
# yet a leak in an image — it was one careless `COPY . .` away from being one.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.env
**/.shoot-token

# **The live production database.** `docker-compose.prod.yml` bind-mounts `./postgres-data`,
# and on the deploy box that is this directory. Postgres owns it uid 999 mode 0700 while the
# runner is `ubuntu`, so the build cannot even stat it: `can't stat '…/postgres-data'`, and the
# rollback step re-runs the same failing command. Multi-gigabyte, unreadable, and needed by
# nothing.
postgres-data

# The backend has its own context (`./backend`), so the frontend image needs none of it —
# except that nothing here may exclude `docs/CROSSVAL_gcsim.md`, which is the whole reason this
# context is the repo root.
backend

# Node / build artifacts
**/node_modules
**/.angular
frontend/dist
frontend/gcsim/gcsim.wasm
frontend/gcsim/wasm_exec.js

# Python artifacts
**/__pycache__
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.venv

# Test and working artifacts
**/coverage
**/.nyc_output
**/data_imports
**/screenshots

# Reference material and scanners
references
security

# Editor / OS
**/.vscode
**/.idea
**/*.swp
**/*.swo
**/.DS_Store
